# loom-server environment file.
#
# Install to /etc/loom/loom-server.env.
# Every variable below is optional except LOOM_UI_DIR: there is no client
# compiled into the binary any more, so a server with no UI source refuses to
# start rather than serving something of its own. The rest have defaults — with
# none of them set the server binds 127.0.0.1:38886 and keeps its log in process
# memory. The values below are the recommended production setup.
#
# systemd reads this file literally (no shell); `KEY=value`, `#` comments, and
# quotes around values with spaces.

# --- listen address -----------------------------------------------------
# host:port. Loopback is the default and the recommended value. Do NOT put a
# public interface here: the API has no authentication and can drive command
# execution on every enrolled machine. Expose it through Tailscale, or through a
# reverse proxy that terminates TLS and authentication, and keep this on
# loopback. See docs/remote-access.md.
LOOM_BIND=127.0.0.1:38886

# --- relay log (choose exactly one) -------------------------------------
# Durable local log: one append-only file per shard under this directory. The
# replay window survives a server restart. Comment this out if you set
# LOOM_REDIS_URL; setting both is a startup error.
LOOM_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/loom/server
# Shared log in Redis Streams. Uncomment for a restart-transparent upgrade
# window shared by more than one node. See docs/redis-backend.md.
#LOOM_REDIS_URL=redis://127.0.0.1:6379

# --- identity -----------------------------------------------------------
# Stamped on every envelope this node produces, so it must be unique per node.
LOOM_NODE_ID=loom-server

# --- UI bundle (required) -----------------------------------------------
# The built product app: the directory `pnpm --filter @bb/app run build` writes,
# which `deploy/install.sh` installs at <prefix>/share/loom/ui — so this default
# is what a default-prefix install produces. Required: there is no client
# compiled into the binary, so a server with neither this nor LOOM_UI_PROXY
# exits at startup. Read-only for the service user.
LOOM_UI_DIR=/usr/local/share/loom/ui
# A frontend dev server to reverse-proxy to instead. Mutually exclusive with
# LOOM_UI_DIR, because two UI sources would make the behaviour depend on
# evaluation order. Development only: it is the Vite dev server of a checkout
# (`pnpm --filter @bb/app run dev`), never a deployed shape.
#LOOM_UI_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:5173

# --- primary host -------------------------------------------------------
# Only for a single-machine deployment: the id of the host running on the
# server's own machine, so primary-host queries prefer it while its daemon is
# attached. Leave unset for a server-only deployment; primary-host resolution
# then falls to connected remote hosts, and answers "no_host" when none exists.
#LOOM_LOCAL_HOST_ID=host_01M...

# --- daemon self-update artifacts ---------------------------------------
# Where this server hosts the daemon binaries that match its own protocol, served
# on GET /install/loom-daemon for a daemon whose protocol does not match. See
# docs/upgrades.md.
#
# Unset (the default) is the directory holding this executable, which is where
# deploy/install.sh puts the matching `loom-daemon` — so an ordinary install
# hosts its own artifacts with nothing to configure here. Set it when the two
# binaries are not side by side, or to host `loom-daemon-<triple>` binaries for
# machines of another architecture. A containerised server carries no daemon and
# so hosts nothing unless this is set.
#LOOM_ARTIFACT_DIR=/usr/local/bin
